# Constraint Satisfaction Problems (CSP) Assignment

Note: The user must have Python already installed on their local machine in order for this program script to run.

This assignment is a program that uses CSPs in order to solve five different sudoku problems, each with varying levels of difficulty.
The difficulty levels are as follows:
* Easy
* Evil
* Medium
* Hard
* Sudoku 01 (given example)

The program uses both a naive and smart backtracking algorithms to solve the puzzles. The smart backtracking using minimum remaining values (MRV), least constraining value (LCV), and forward checking (FC) in order to solve the puzzles.
--------------------------------
## How to execute:
* Clone this repo from GitHub using `git clone https://github.com/emirick72/CS-580_Sudoku-Puzzle_Assignment.git`
* `cd` into the repo on your machine (`cd CS-580_Sudoku-Puzzle_Assignment`)
* Command to run the program (in the terminal only, only runs for the "Sudoku_01.txt" puzzle): `python main.py`
* Command for generating the results into `benchmark_results.txt`: `python -m src.benchmark`